WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.923
- Worth It.

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:01.756
- Philadelphia.

00:00:01.756 --> 00:00:02.914
- Cheesesteaks.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.180
- [Steven] Today on Worth It we're gonna be trying

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.880
three awesome Philadelphia cheesesteaks

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.490
at three drastically different price points

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.100
to find out which one is the most worth it at its price.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.720
^- As you can see, we're joined here today by Quinta B.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.640
- Hello!

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.625
I am here today because, fun fact, I am from Philadelphia.

00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:17.930
- Quinta, who is that?

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.240
- That is William Penn,

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.624
founder of Pennsylvania

00:00:21.624 --> 00:00:25.573
and initiator of brotherly love in Philadelphia.

00:00:25.573 --> 00:00:27.470
- [Steven] Oh, that's right, the city of brotherly love.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.303
- Let's do it!

00:00:28.303 --> 00:00:29.370
- Cheesesteaks!
- Worth It.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.000
^- How you doing today?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.010
^My name's Jo Clementi.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.620
^I'm the general manager of John's Roast Pork.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.510
We're in South Philadelphia, Snyder Avenue.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.070
I'll be making you both our traditional pork Italian

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.340
and our south philly cheesesteak.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.943
John's family's been here since 1930.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.040
It just started as a local truck stop.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.810
It's a family style operation.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.710
- I've never had a cheesesteak from here,

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.690
so I'm really excited.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.530
I'm from West Philly,

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.363
so I've mainly gotten mine

00:00:51.363 --> 00:00:52.690
from corner stores in West Philly.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.700
- They're all very good, it's just depends on the time.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.630
Sometimes at midnight you're heading out, you get done,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.860
and you wanna get something to eat,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.673
and I pass by the same spots and I get the same thing.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.690
Your steak doesn't go on the grill until you order.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.660
You tell me what your sandwich it, how you like it:

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.900
American, mild, or sharp provolone, and make it like that.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.930
Takes a few extra minutes,

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.830
but people seem like they like it better that way.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:11.663
- [Steven] Okay.

00:01:11.663 --> 00:01:13.460
Oh my God, it's really steaming there.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.940
Whoa!
- It's beautiful.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.643
- Whoa, cheers.

00:01:16.821 --> 00:01:18.039
- Wow.
- Ew!

00:01:18.039 --> 00:01:19.615
(laughing)

00:01:19.615 --> 00:01:21.448
- Welcome to Worth It.

00:01:22.228 --> 00:01:24.395
(moaning)

00:01:26.273 --> 00:01:27.623
- This is what we came for.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.483
- This is one of those foods

00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:31.353
that's a little bit more carnal, if you know what I mean.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.310
You know, it's messy.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.886
- It's kinda like the ice cream sundae of meats.

00:01:35.886 --> 00:01:38.940
There's like a fudge sauce with the cheese,

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.010
there's different little things you could dress it up with.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.470
It's in this kinda...
- Different toppings.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.683
- Banana shape.
- Yup.

00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:46.060
A cheesesteak is the mistake you make on purpose.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.380
We know we're gonna feel bad after this.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.460
Right now, isn't it bringing you so much joy?

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.600
- Is this representative of a cheesesteak in Philly?

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.790
- Yeah, 100%.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.400
The cheese is perfect, the steak is cut very nicely,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.530
the bread is good too.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.710
It's not even an Amoroso roll,

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.410
which is what most Philly cheesesteaks are made on.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.410
It just has to be good bread, good steak.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.460
Made with love, if you will.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:05.293
- We're gonna have a bite of this pork now,

00:02:05.293 --> 00:02:07.200
just to see what it's all about.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.210
- In South Philly, for Italian,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.980
we grew up in the way that we always had pork,

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.210
our mother'd make 'em back and forth

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.074
because of the price and stuff like that.

00:02:14.074 --> 00:02:15.330
Because growing up it was obviously

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.520
cheaper than filet mignon.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.353
In South Philadelphia,

00:02:17.353 --> 00:02:19.260
you can go on any corner and get some type of cheesesteak,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.980
but to get a roast pork, there's only a few spots.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.474
We're very luck to have both products

00:02:23.474 --> 00:02:25.273
that it seems like everybody likes.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.673
- Pork, roasted.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.660
- I want, I want, I want.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.013
Thank you.

00:02:32.727 --> 00:02:35.220
- [Andrew] Oh, a little spicy with those peppers on there.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.260
- And you guys weren't allowed

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.103
to see how this is seasoned, right?

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.805
- No, it's a little bit of a secret.

00:02:39.805 --> 00:02:40.638
A little bit.
- I like that.

00:02:40.638 --> 00:02:41.471
I love a good secret.

00:02:41.471 --> 00:02:45.830
- Delicious spiced pork, slowly roasted and juicy.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.430
Steven, you have to eat two more cheesesteaks today.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.390
You will regret that.

00:02:51.649 --> 00:02:52.535
(mumbling)

00:02:52.535 --> 00:02:53.368
- He looks like a dumpster.

00:02:53.368 --> 00:02:55.170
How can you just eat...

00:02:58.559 --> 00:02:59.830
- So, we got some canolis

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.600
at this well-renowned bakery called Isgro's.

00:03:02.669 --> 00:03:04.180
Look at this, you know what one of my favorite things is?

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.470
- The packaging.
- This string.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.623
- [Quinta] It's classy and classic.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.140
- Actually recommended by

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.940
^your friend and mine, Kate Peterman.

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:19.434
^- Isgro's.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.699
^- Yeah.
- Yeah, it's so good.

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:21.560
- They taste like Christmas.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.047
I said this is why Kate likes it.

00:03:23.047 --> 00:03:25.323
^- You see what it looks like?
- Hey, Garrett!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.573
Yes, yes, it is.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.913
- [All] Yes, yes.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:30.220
- But Adam is gonna eat it.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.053
- For you.

00:03:32.421 --> 00:03:33.638
(laughing)

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.333
^- Hey, Kate, watch this.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.093
^- [Quinta] Adam!

00:03:37.093 --> 00:03:37.926
Adam.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.053
- Oh.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:41.000
- Wow, I'm so sorry.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:41.833
We gotta go.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.023
^Bye, Kate, I love you.

00:03:43.093 --> 00:03:44.000
- Bye.
- Bye.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.410
- Thanks for the recommendation.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.210
So, now we're on our way to our second cheesesteak stop.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.970
This one is gonna be a little bit out of the ordinary.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.213
There's no steak in this cheesesteak.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.483
It may, technically, be acceptable for a vegetarian to eat.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.780
- See, this is why I don't do stuff like this.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.663
Y'all always have surprises.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.160
^- My name is Josh Noh.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.340
^I'm originally from Delaware,

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.230
^I've lived in Philadelphia for 16 years,

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.427
and today I'm gonna prepare for you

00:04:09.427 --> 00:04:10.880
the Philly mushroom cheesesteak.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.500
Gin &amp; Pop is a bar with high craft cocktails

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:14.660
and elevated bar food.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.760
The motivation behind the menu,

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.570
it's basically fine dine cooking all day,

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.403
eating junk food at night.

00:04:18.403 --> 00:04:21.020
A combination of two of what a like and taking bits

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.326
and pieces and executing it with fine dining technique.

00:04:23.326 --> 00:04:25.730
- So, your cheesesteak has no steak.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.613
What was the decision behind that?

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.690
- We're not just cooking for carnivores,

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.910
we're cooking for everybody.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.870
A mushroom is the meat of a vegetarian, it's 80% water,

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.000
so you can draw the water out

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.823
and then put back in more flavor.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.140
We start off slowly caramelizing fennel and shallot.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.550
After that's got a nice color,

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.890
then you draw the sugars out of the onion, add the mushroom.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.210
The mushrooms I select are usually

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.070
oyster, cremini, and shiitake, the triple combination.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.280
Let that entirely cook down,

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.770
make a little fondue with taleggio, a little parmesan,

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.350
the roasted garlic, the residual heat from the mushrooms,

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.929
and it melts into this gooey mushroom mass.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.810
Heat it up with slices of cheese on it,

00:04:58.810 --> 00:04:59.800
throw it in the oven,

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.113
slide it on top of the baguette with a little bit

00:05:01.113 --> 00:05:02.993
of arugula and pickled shallots.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.550
- We're at a bar, so even though we're in Philly,

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:06.733
I got a Manhattan.

00:05:06.747 --> 00:05:07.580
- [All] Cheers.

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.230
- (clears throat) Sorry.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.170
- The drinks are good.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.603
- [Both] The Philly cheesesteak.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.633
- Quinta, I'm sorry.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:20.340
Quinta didn't know that we were gonna be doing this today.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.220
I mean, she knew that we were gonna

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.110
have a bunch of cheesesteaks,

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.503
but she didn't know that we'd be having a vegetarian one.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.383
- You know, can't take the magic outta Disneyland.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.430
It's just a land, so, this is just...

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.021
But we'll see.
- Cheers.

00:05:33.021 --> 00:05:34.173
- Cheers.

00:05:39.527 --> 00:05:40.360
Mm!

00:05:40.684 --> 00:05:42.808
- Are you kidding me?
(laughing)

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:45.283
Quinta, eat your sandwich.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:47.723
- Yo, that's...

00:05:47.723 --> 00:05:48.920
I'm not missing the steak at all.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.050
- So, you guys like it a lot?

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.700
- I'm not gonna lie, I love this.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.660
It seems like he's composed this amazing

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.470
mushroom combination to mimic perfectly what you get

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:01.050
when you bite into an actual Philly cheesesteak.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.009
- Quinta is not impressed

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:02.842
at all.
- I'm not.

00:06:02.842 --> 00:06:03.675
- It is tasty.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:04.970
- It's tasty, it's very tasty.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.270
- It's messy, but it's light.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.100
I feel good.
- It is light, it's good.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.070
The bread's good, the truffle's amazing,

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.170
the mushrooms are done right.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.003
- What about the cheese?

00:06:12.003 --> 00:06:13.530
- The cheese is great.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.360
- So, Quinta, I feel like I'm slowly getting you to admit

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.010
that this is a great cheesesteak sandwich.

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.290
- Listen, I would recommend this to any person

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.850
who is looking for a great vegetarian meal.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.270
They're different, that's all I'm saying.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.610
This is not a cheesesteak.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.457
- This is like you had a fantastic cheesesteak sandwich,

00:06:29.457 --> 00:06:31.600
but then you just omitted the steak

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.083
and doubled the mushrooms.
- Yeah, true.

00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:36.370
- I agree that nothing can quite replace the taste of steak.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.203
- Thank you.

00:06:38.355 --> 00:06:39.188
Thank you.
- I mean,

00:06:39.188 --> 00:06:40.450
look at a cow and look at a mushroom.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.973
- I've seen 'em both, and I want to eat the cow.

00:06:42.983 --> 00:06:45.233
(laughing)

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:49.853
- Gin &amp; Pop.

00:06:49.853 --> 00:06:51.819
All things considered, pretty good sandwich.

00:06:51.819 --> 00:06:52.652
- Yeah.

00:06:52.652 --> 00:06:53.701
- Yeah, it was great, yeah.
- Steven.

00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:54.951
(mumbling)

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.425
- I do love little vegetarian change-ups

00:06:56.425 --> 00:06:59.580
every once in a while.
- I notoriously despite them.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.412
Hit us with a food fact, Steven!

00:07:01.412 --> 00:07:02.660
- Philly cheesesteak fact!

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:06.770
^In 2015, the inaugural Philadephia Cheesesteak Festival

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:11.230
^kicked off with a 450 foot long Philly cheesesteak.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.063
^- [Andrew] Wow.

00:07:12.063 --> 00:07:13.110
- That's a lot of cheesesteak.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.680
- I always ask why.
(laughing)

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.200
Why make a cheesesteak that long?

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.918
- Because...
- What're you trying to prove?

00:07:18.918 --> 00:07:19.990
- That's not trying to prove anything.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.220
It's for the love of the game.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.660
- Yeah, humans have always done that.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:23.820
They're like, I love q thing,

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:24.960
I'm gonna make the biggest version of it.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.793
- Exactly.

00:07:25.793 --> 00:07:26.920
- The Egyptians loved triangles.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.220
- That's how we got Texas.

00:07:28.337 --> 00:07:30.587
(laughing)

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:31.970
- That's how we got Texas?

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.300
- Yeah, they loved states so much they were like,

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.610
we're gonna make a big version of it

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.260
and then Texas happened.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.780
- We're on our way to a new place, a last place,

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:43.382
called Barclay Prime?
- Barclay Prime.

00:07:43.382 --> 00:07:45.038
- Steakhouse.
- Yeah.

00:07:45.038 --> 00:07:47.760
- Pretty excited they're gonna do a twist

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.670
on a Philly cheesesteak by adding lots of stuff on it

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.550
that'll cost a lot of money, so...

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.760
- The twist is it's gonna cost a lot of money.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.270
